{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 49, :comments ["<b>He sent</b> — an allusion to the abundance of their terror from the plague of hail, as he said, \"all the plagues of Elohim upon your heart,\" and did not Pharaoh ever confess, saying: \"I and my people are the wicked,\" except in this plague. And behold, he likened these plagues to the wrath of HaShem, and the sending of evil angels because of the fire, like \"He makes His angels winds, His ministers flaming fire.\"" "<b>And the word \"His angels\"</b> — is not in construct state, as though written: \"the angels of HaShem,\" like \"by the hand of prophets, every seer.\""], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 78, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:35:15.469989434Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}